# Snyk (https://snyk.io) policy file: recorded risk acceptances, reviewed in PRs (PLAN.md §2.6).
# Every entry needs a reason and an expiry. `snyk ignore` rewrites this file and drops comments,
# so the full analysis lives in each `reason`.
version: v1.25.0
ignore:
  SNYK-JS-BRACES-19963945:
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          WHAT: braces <=3.0.3 has recursive AST walkers with no depth guard. A deeply nested
          brace pattern (still under the length limit) overflows the call stack and crashes the
          Node process with a RangeError. Availability only: no data read or changed.
          NO FIX: 3.0.3 (May 2024) is the newest braces release, so there is nothing to
          upgrade, patch or pnpm-override to.
          HOW IT REACHES US: only apps/mobile, and only through build and test tooling:
          react-native > @react-native/community-cli-plugin > metro > metro-file-map >
          micromatch > braces, plus jest / babel-jest / eslint-plugin-jest > micromatch > braces.
          Metro is the bundler that runs on a developer machine or CI; it is not part of the JS
          bundle shipped in the app, and Jest/ESLint never run on a phone.
          EXPLOITABILITY: an attacker would need to control a glob pattern passed to micromatch.
          Ours come only from repo config (metro.config.js, Jest and ESLint config), never from
          network or user input. Worst case, a malicious commit crashes a local build, and a
          malicious commit can already run arbitrary code at build time anyway.
          API NOT AFFECTED: apps/api has no path to braces (`pnpm why braces --filter @lern/api`
          is empty as of 2026-10-19). The '*' path also covers future paths, so if the api ever
          pulls braces in, re-check before renewing.
          REVISIT: at expiry; sooner if braces publishes a fix (upgrade, delete this entry) or if
          any server code starts passing user input to micromatch/braces (then it's a real DoS).
        expires: 2027-01-17T00:00:00.000Z
        created: 2026-10-19T00:00:00.000Z
  SNYK-JS-PICOMATCH-21248802:
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          WHAT: picomatch ReDoS (CVE-2026-112366, CWE-1333, published 2026-10-19). A crafted
          glob pattern makes picomatch build a regex with catastrophic backtracking and hangs the
          process. Availability only: no data read or changed.
          NO FIX: 4.0.7 and 2.3.2 are the newest releases of each line and Snyk lists no fixed
          version, so there is nothing to upgrade, patch or pnpm-override to.
          HOW IT REACHES US: only build and test tooling (32 paths): react-native >
          @react-native/codegen > tinyglobby, metro > micromatch / anymatch, jest-util,
          jest-haste-map, @parcel/watcher. None of it ships in the app bundle.
          EXPLOITABILITY: same as the braces entry above: patterns come only from repo config
          (metro, Jest, ESLint, codegen), never from network or user input.
          REVISIT: at expiry; sooner if picomatch publishes a fix (upgrade, delete this entry).
        expires: 2027-01-19T00:00:00.000Z
        created: 2026-10-21T00:00:00.000Z
  SNYK-JS-OPEN-22112123:
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          WHAT: open <11.0.0 (CVE-2026-119025, CWE-116, published 2026-11-01). Per Snyk's advisory
          the Windows launch path builds a shell command from the target without escaping it, so a
          caller that passes an attacker-influenced target can have the command altered.
          WHERE THE FLAW RUNS: only on Windows or WSL. Both installed copies were read: open@8.4.2
          takes the PowerShell branch only when `platform === 'win32'` or WSL, open@6.4.0 takes the
          `cmd /c start` branch on the same condition. On macOS and Linux both spawn `open` /
          `xdg-open` with an argument array and no shell.
          HOW IT REACHES US: only React Native's dev server, in apps/mobile: @react-native-community/cli
          > cli-server-api > open@6.4.0 (the `/open-url` endpoint) and react-native >
          community-cli-plugin > dev-middleware > open@8.4.2 (opens the debugger window). It runs on
          a developer machine while Metro is up; it is not in the app bundle. Development is on
          macOS, and CI (Linux) never starts the dev server, so the flawed branch is unreachable.
          NO COMPATIBLE FIX: 11.0.0 is the only fixed line. The newest tooling still asks for the
          old ones (dev-middleware 0.88.1: ^8.4.2, cli-server-api 21.0.0: ^6.2.0). A pnpm override
          to 11 was tried on 2026-11-16: open 11 is ESM-only, so dev-middleware's
          `const open = require("open"); open(url)` fallback gets an object and throws.
          API NOT AFFECTED: `pnpm why open --filter @lern/api` is empty as of 2026-11-16.
          REVISIT: at expiry; sooner if React Native or its CLI moves to open >=11 (upgrade, delete
          this entry), or if anyone develops on Windows or WSL (then fix before running Metro there).
        expires: 2027-02-14T00:00:00.000Z
        created: 2026-11-16T00:00:00.000Z
  SNYK-RUBY-ACTIVESUPPORT-22839999:
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          WHAT: activesupport <8.0.5.2 (CVE-2026-126080, GHSA-8474-xrp6-wh69, High,
          Executable Regular Expression Error).
          NO COMPATIBLE FIX: 7.2.4 is the newest 7.x release and Snyk lists 8.0.5.2 as the
          first fixed version. All cocoapods-core releases through the latest (1.17.0) require
          activesupport (>= 5.0, < 8), so Bundler cannot install 8.0.5.2 alongside CocoaPods.
          HOW IT REACHES US: apps/mobile/Gemfile.lock locks activesupport@7.2.4 directly and
          through cocoapods@1.15.2 > cocoapods-core@1.15.2 > activesupport@7.2.4. This
          Gemfile.lock is for mobile iOS only. CocoaPods is build-time tooling that runs on
          developer Macs during pod install and is never bundled in the mobile app or API.
          EXPLOITABILITY: the repo has no Rails or Action Cable runtime, and no untrusted
          input reaches activesupport.
          REVISIT: at expiry, or sooner if CocoaPods supports activesupport 8.x or a fixed
          7.2.x backport ships.
        expires: 2027-02-23T00:00:00.000Z
        created: 2026-11-25T00:00:00.000Z
patch: {}
